Subject: [SE3-P5] winedmo: activate all selected streams before starting

media_source_start() activated streams one at a time while the demux
thread was already reading, so the first packets of a later-index stream
could be dropped as belonging to an inactive stream (seen as a lost leading
ALAC block, worst case a lost first video GOP). When starting from STOPPED,
mark every selected stream active before the per-stream start loop, holding
all stream queue locks at once: the demux thread checks whether any stream
is active, and drops a packet for an inactive one, under those locks, so it
cannot observe a partial activation.

---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/media_source.c
@@ -1399,6 +1399,20 @@
         return hr;
     }
 
+    /* The demux thread reads once any stream is active and drops a packet whose
+     * stream is inactive, checking both under the stream queue locks. Activate
+     * every selected stream while holding all of them, so that no later stream
+     * can still be inactive when the first packets arrive. */
+    if (starting)
+    {
+        for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
+            EnterCriticalSection(&source->streams[i]->queue_cs);
+        for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
+            source->streams[i]->active = !!descriptors[i];
+        for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
+            LeaveCriticalSection(&source->streams[i]->queue_cs);
+    }
+
     for (i = 0; i < source->stream_count; i++)
     {
         struct media_stream *stream = source->streams[i];
